      "id": "GI1A-R3-04",
      "detail": "Factory contract_admission is selected only from E1/E2 slot types and ignores e2_admission; an E2 typed-present mapping with terminal_deferred admission is incorrectly promoted to declared_consistent. Minimal fix: require e2_admission == :declared_consistent for declared_consistent, otherwise retain terminal_deferred.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "line": 409,
          "text": "    e2, e2_admission, e2_gaps = _gi1_e2_slot(package, e0, n06)"
        },
        {
          "line": 414,
          "text": "    admission = e1 isa GI1N05PresentAuthoritySlotV1 &&"
        },
        {
          "line": 424,
          "text": "        contract_admission=admission, physical_resolution=terminal_deferred,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GI1A-R3-05",
      "detail": "Factory maps every n05_check status other than valid to ArgumentError; n05_check.status == :program_exception is therefore misclassified as fail_closed instead of retaining program_exception. Minimal fix: branch program_exception before the fail_closed ArgumentError path and preserve that taxonomy through the trusted API.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "line": 405,
          "text": "        n05_check.status === :valid ||"
        },
        {
          "line": 406,
          "text": "            throw(ArgumentError(\"GI1 E1 source fail_closed: \" * join(n05_check.errors, \",\")))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "GI1A-R3-06",
      "detail": "R3 tests do not execute the explicit N06 typed-present/deferred branch and do not directly test exception taxonomy; the current-A baseline has no valid N06 mapping positive. Minimal fix: add a structurally valid source-bound mapping fixture only to exercise typed E2-present plus terminal_deferred, and add targeted program_exception classification controls without claiming a physical positive.",
